From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:56:57 +0200
Subject: net: dsa: lantiq: let a model finish the switch bring-up

setup() covers the blocks the whole family shares, and the reset it issues
first returns everything else in the switch register window to its defaults.
A model whose window holds more than those blocks therefore cannot program
them from probe: whatever it writes there is undone by the time setup()
returns.

Add a per-model setup callback, run at the end of setup() in the same shape as
the existing per-port one, so a model can place its own bring-up after the
reset, the microcode load and the MDIO bus registration.

No functional change: no existing model sets the callback.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/lantiq_gswip.h b/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/lantiq_gswip.h
index 343dac7a1625..2d973f348593 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/lantiq_gswip.h
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/lantiq_gswip.h
@@ -316,6 +316,12 @@ struct gswip_hw_info {
 	struct phylink_pcs *(*mac_select_pcs)(struct phylink_config *config,
 					      phy_interface_t interface);
 	int (*port_setup)(struct dsa_switch *ds, int port);
+	/* Model-specific part of the switch bring-up. Runs at the end of
+	 * setup(), after the microcode load and the MDIO bus registration,
+	 * so a model can program blocks that the reset at the start of
+	 * setup() returns to their defaults.
+	 */
+	int (*setup)(struct dsa_switch *ds);
 };
 
 struct gswip_gphy_fw {
diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/lantiq_gswip_common.c b/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/lantiq_gswip_common.c
index 8cf031279496..b92d15d063c1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/lantiq_gswip_common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/lantiq_gswip_common.c
@@ -794,6 +794,12 @@ static int gswip_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
 
 	ds->mtu_enforcement_ingress = true;
 
+	if (priv->hw_info->setup) {
+		err = priv->hw_info->setup(ds);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
